  "releaseNotes": "v1.4.1 - Documentation only.\n\nNo functional change. Not one selector, setter or resource key differs from v1.4.0; the assembly differs only by its embedded version stamp.\n\nThe README now documents how to wire the sidebar to pages, which it previously left to the reader. It covers the pattern itself - one list of pages driving both the navigation buttons and the content area, so adding a page is a single line - and where a Dependency Injection Container plugs in, if you use one. It also explains why that shape, by naming the two mistakes the obvious alternative invites, neither of which produces an exception or a binding error.\n\nUpgrade only if you want the documentation. If v1.4.0 works for you, nothing here changes it.",
